==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|югъ||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
Traditionally explained as borrowing from Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|югъ}} {{der|ru|sla-pro|*jugъ}}, compare {{cog|orv|угъ}}. However, self-innovation is also possible, compare the prosthetic /й/ in loanwords or in words that had no iotation in Church Slavonic: dialectal {{m|ru|ю́дега}} 'hoarfrost' from Finnish {{m|fi|huude}}, use of a preposition {{m|ru|у}} like /ю/ in some northern Russian dialects, and dialectal {{m|ru|юрод}} in the presence of the Church Slavonic {{m|cu|Ѫродъ}}.<ref>Andrey Zaliznyak. Drevnenovgorodskij dialekt. Jazyki slavjanskoj kul'tury: Moskva. 2004. page 54</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-юг.ogg}}

